;; The pill's state, one JSON object per line, straight off the daemon's socket.
;;
;; A loop rather than the `sleep 5` this used to open with. That delay was there
;; because the launcher was spawned by the compositor at login and the socket did
;; not exist yet; the daemon is a user unit now and binds both sockets before its
;; first request, so what is left to handle is the daemon restarting -- after
;; which socat exits and this reconnects a second later. The other pills get the
;; same behaviour from their CLI's own retry loop; this one has no CLI, so it is
;; here.
(deflisten hass-lamp :initial '{"state":"loading"}'
  "while true; do socat -u UNIX-CLIENT:$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hass/state.sock -; sleep 1; done")
